# ROTKA Case Study Content Integrity

Case-study content is evidence, not filler.

## Absolute rule
Never create user-visible project content unless it exists in an explicitly approved source.

When an approved content file exists:
- import/read from that source
- do not duplicate or paraphrase it elsewhere
- do not add helpful-sounding text
- do not fill missing slots

## Forbidden invention
Do not invent headings, subheads, captions, annotations, labels, metadata, metrics, findings, research, personas, quotes, results, outcomes, validation, technical architecture, workflows presented as fact, screens, diagrams, or feature names.

If the design needs content that does not exist:
OMIT THE DESIGN ELEMENT.

## Diff check
Before finishing:
- inspect changed frontend files for newly introduced user-visible strings
- every new case-study string must map to the approved content source
- if any string cannot be traced to approved content, remove it

Report explicitly:
CONTENT INVENTION CHECK: PASS
or
CONTENT INVENTION CHECK: FAIL
